1
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:08,840
Thank you.

2
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:03,840
Alright.

3
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:05,480
You drank it all.

4
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:06,240
You,

5
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:07,440
and you,

6
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:09,060
go out and buy a bottle.

7
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:18,480
You too.

8
00:02:18,720 --> 00:02:19,250
Let's go.

9
00:02:19,520 --> 00:02:20,120
Hurry up.

10
00:02:22,079 --> 00:02:22,880
And you.

11
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:24,280
Go.

12
00:02:37,280 --> 00:02:38,160
Have you been

13
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:40,090
really annoyed with me lately?

14
00:02:42,360 --> 00:02:43,720
I haven't.

15
00:02:44,079 --> 00:02:44,920
Then swear.

16
00:02:45,079 --> 00:02:46,280
If you are,

17
00:02:46,480 --> 00:02:48,079
you'll never make any money.

18
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:50,360
Why should I swear?

19
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:51,960
Then you are.

20
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:54,000
Why?

21
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:57,760
It's my own problem.

22
00:02:58,800 --> 00:02:59,840
The bag is heavy. Let me help.

23
00:02:59,840 --> 00:03:00,600
No need.

24
00:03:02,160 --> 00:03:04,560
It hurts me when you act like this suddenly.

25
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:06,170
Why does it hurt you?

26
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:08,960
I hate it when you're like this.

27
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:11,080
No.

28
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,480
Why are you so nice to everyone?

29
00:03:14,880 --> 00:03:15,320
Why do you care

30
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:16,960
about everyone's feelings?

31
00:03:18,880 --> 00:03:20,079
You're nice to

32
00:03:20,480 --> 00:03:21,280
Yiyi,

33
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:23,600
and to Zhao Tianfang.

34
00:03:25,480 --> 00:03:26,440
They're my colleagues

35
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:28,560
and clients. It's my job.

36
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:29,400
Fine.

37
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:31,620
Then what about my sister?

38
00:03:32,440 --> 00:03:35,400
Why are you serving tea and water to my sister

39
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:37,000
and showing so much concern?

40
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:40,320
Because...

41
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:42,160
Because...

42
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:44,560
Because I have my difficulties.

43
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:46,400
Because you have ulterior motives,

44
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:47,079
right?

45
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:48,680
What ulterior motives?

46
00:03:48,680 --> 00:03:50,040
I have my difficulties.

47
00:03:50,160 --> 00:03:51,290
What difficulties?

48
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:57,360
You can't make anything up, can you?

49
00:03:57,840 --> 00:03:59,370
Because I'm Golden Spiral.

50
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:03,880
The client who wrote the bad review

51
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:06,000
and got you fired was me.

52
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:07,960
And

53
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:11,090
I also ruined your sister's divorce photoshoot.

54
00:04:11,640 --> 00:04:13,400
So I stayed to compensate her.

55
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:15,680
I supported her and treated her well

56
00:04:15,680 --> 00:04:17,160
because I was afraid she'd tell you,

57
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:18,440
and you'd ignore me.

58
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:22,760
I...

59
00:04:23,280 --> 00:04:25,480
I was also afraid it would affect our work.

60
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:27,610
I was worried about my year-end bonus.

61
00:04:29,960 --> 00:04:30,840
So,

62
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:32,960
I want to have a good talk with you.

63
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:33,520
Talk?

64
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:35,800
Go ahead.

65
00:04:36,520 --> 00:04:37,960
If you put money aside,

66
00:04:39,040 --> 00:04:40,700
what do you want to talk about?

67
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:46,560
Can you put money aside?

68
00:04:50,960 --> 00:04:51,760
True.

69
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:54,920
Wait for me.

70
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:56,000
Wait for you to do what?

71
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,640
Wait for you to write me a bad review?

72
00:04:57,640 --> 00:04:58,000
What are you doing?

73
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:59,200
I'll carry it for you.

74
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:01,000
I don't need you to carry it. Give it to me.

75
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,280
You wrote a 2,000-word bad review.

76
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:03,880
How dare you even speak to me?

77
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:06,000
That was written by AI.

78
00:05:07,280 --> 00:05:08,280
Written by AI?

79
00:05:08,280 --> 00:05:10,080
You think you're so great?

80
00:05:10,160 --> 00:05:11,360
Let's go.

81
00:05:19,080 --> 00:05:20,680
What's so urgent

82
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:22,800
that you have to call me over in the middle of the night?

83
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:23,720
Keep it down.

84
00:05:23,840 --> 00:05:25,120
Don't let her hear you.

85
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:28,700
Come in.

86
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:30,000
Xinyue,

87
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,880
here are the Honglai chicken feet you wanted.

88
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:33,640
They are super spicy.

89
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:35,130
Keep it down.

90
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:38,930
Come inside.

91
00:05:41,080 --> 00:05:42,520
That's what happened.

92
00:05:42,960 --> 00:05:45,400
After she found out I'm Golden Spiral,

93
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:47,640
she seems a bit angry.

94
00:05:48,360 --> 00:05:49,890
Are you sure it's just a bit?

95
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:53,800
I'm so mad!

96
00:05:54,400 --> 00:05:55,680
I found out later

97
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:56,960
that he's the jerk

98
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:58,600
who forced me to resign.

99
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:02,320
But he's been running around helping you lately.

100
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:04,240
At least he tried his best.

101
00:06:05,080 --> 00:06:05,920
So,

102
00:06:06,880 --> 00:06:07,880
she should forgive me.

103
00:06:07,880 --> 00:06:09,160
Fifty percent?

104
00:06:09,880 --> 00:06:10,880
Thirty percent?

105
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:12,960
At least fifteen percent?

106
00:06:13,520 --> 00:06:14,360
In his dreams.

107
00:06:15,760 --> 00:06:16,680
Besides,

108
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:18,960
if it weren't for my accidental push,

109
00:06:18,960 --> 00:06:21,080
how could she have started her own business?

110
00:06:21,080 --> 00:06:23,320
Just for this trivial matter,

111
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:24,760
she's acting like this with me.

112
00:06:24,760 --> 00:06:27,200
I'm not angry about the Golden Spiral thing.

113
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:28,720
I just can't stand him as a person.

114
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:30,720
Besides, I didn't even provoke her.

115
00:06:30,840 --> 00:06:32,840
I think I treat her pretty well,

116
00:06:32,880 --> 00:06:35,610
always checking in on her and serving her drinks.

117
00:06:38,080 --> 00:06:40,920
He doesn't understand women at all.

118
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:43,000
Why pretend to be a sweet guy?

119
00:06:43,159 --> 00:06:45,080
He flirts with everyone.

120
00:06:45,080 --> 00:06:45,960
You be the judge.

121
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:48,000
Is it a crime to be a good guy?

122
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,260
I really don't know what she's thinking.

123
00:06:51,760 --> 00:06:52,600
Why are you crying?

124
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:53,480
Please don't cry.

125
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:54,640
Listen to that.

126
00:06:54,760 --> 00:06:57,200
She's crying just because of this.

127
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:58,360
What's the fuss?

128
00:06:58,360 --> 00:07:00,020
It's just from the spicy food.

129
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:04,120
Am I really that unforgivable?

130
00:07:05,760 --> 00:07:06,720
How about

131
00:07:06,720 --> 00:07:08,240
you schedule a time to have a good talk with her?

132
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:09,400
She's fuming right now.

133
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:10,080
If I ask her out,

134
00:07:10,080 --> 00:07:11,680
she'll tear me to pieces.

135
00:07:11,960 --> 00:07:12,640
True.

136
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:16,300
What are you holding in your hand?

137
00:07:16,960 --> 00:07:18,680
Nothing, just a ring.

138
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:20,500
I won it in a lucky draw.

139
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:23,420
A lucky draw gave you such a beautiful women's ring?

140
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:26,040
You didn't buy it yourself, did you?

141
00:07:26,520 --> 00:07:26,920
Then...

142
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:28,280
How is that possible?

143
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:30,840
Saving money is my lifelong priority.

144
00:07:30,840 --> 00:07:31,600
How could I possibly

145
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:33,860
spend money on such impractical things?

146
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:36,860
It's obvious he did it on purpose.

147
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:39,200
Let me be clear.

148
00:07:39,840 --> 00:07:40,840
Unless...

149
00:07:41,080 --> 00:07:41,920
unless he

150
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:43,320
sincerely,

151
00:07:43,640 --> 00:07:44,800
proactively,

152
00:07:45,159 --> 00:07:47,320
and earnestly apologizes to me.

153
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:51,159
Otherwise, I definitely won't be nice to him.

154
00:07:51,159 --> 00:07:51,560
Right.

155
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:53,159
Let's hold off for now.

156
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:54,760
When she softens up a bit,

157
00:07:54,920 --> 00:07:56,640
you can have a good talk with her.

158
00:07:56,640 --> 00:07:59,700
After all, it's better to make peace than hold grudges.

159
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:00,600
Okay.

160
00:08:00,880 --> 00:08:03,240
Then we'll just wait and see.

161
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:05,240
Eat less.

162
00:08:05,440 --> 00:08:07,040
You'll be bloated tomorrow.

163
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:09,610
This is so annoying.

164
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:11,640
Why give a women's ring for a raffle?

165
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:13,080
Then just give it to her.

166
00:08:13,080 --> 00:08:15,080
Wouldn't it be nice to do her a favor?

167
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:17,720
Let's do that.

168
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:26,290
Morning.

169
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:28,090
Morning.

170
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:30,480
How come it's you?

171
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:35,240
Then where is she?

172
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,360
Xinyue went out for an interview today.

173
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:41,600
Yiying went to the homestay.

174
00:08:41,840 --> 00:08:43,960
So I'm filling in for the shift today.

175
00:08:44,680 --> 00:08:46,210
Then why didn't you call me?

176
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:48,760
That difficult customer from last time

177
00:08:48,880 --> 00:08:51,200
wrote a really long positive review for you two.

178
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:53,530
Now the shop is getting busier and busier.

179
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:55,080
By the way.

180
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:58,360
Xinyue said she arranged other work for you today.

181
00:08:58,640 --> 00:08:59,640
Other work.

182
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:01,920
What kind of work is other work?

183
00:09:01,920 --> 00:09:02,320
Here.

184
00:09:05,160 --> 00:09:06,160
Welcome aboard.

185
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:13,480
Isn't this the guy who sells Honglai chicken feet?

186
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:14,800
Why did you bring him here?

187
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:16,400
Do we have any business dealings with him?

188
00:09:16,400 --> 00:09:17,330
You mean Qin Fei?

189
00:09:18,640 --> 00:09:20,960
His grandfather is going to sell chicken feet with Yuzhen next door,

190
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:22,160
so he was called here.

191
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:32,140
I am a minor shareholder at least.

192
00:09:32,160 --> 00:09:33,640
Even if you want to hire someone new,

193
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:35,040
you should tell me first.

194
00:09:35,040 --> 00:09:36,040
I did tell you.

195
00:09:36,440 --> 00:09:37,160
I told you yesterday.

196
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:40,040
I said someone was coming for an interview this morning.

197
00:09:40,040 --> 00:09:41,000
Look at him.

198
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:42,800
He is pleasing to the eye.

199
00:09:42,880 --> 00:09:44,480
What a great value for money.

200
00:09:51,160 --> 00:09:52,880
Li Xinyue, can you not be so superficial?

201
00:09:52,880 --> 00:09:54,360
We are in the early stage of our startup.

202
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:56,000
You're expanding so blindly.

203
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:57,480
Just to see some muscles,

204
00:09:57,480 --> 00:09:59,480
you're spending thousands more a month.

205
00:09:59,480 --> 00:10:01,680
Who exactly is superficial between us?

206
00:10:03,360 --> 00:10:03,920
You,

207
00:10:04,800 --> 00:10:05,360
Mr. Qin.

208
00:10:05,800 --> 00:10:06,160
I...

209
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:07,340
I remember you.

210
00:10:07,680 --> 00:10:08,760
That day, you and Xinyue

211
00:10:08,760 --> 00:10:10,680
came to our stall to buy chicken feet.

212
00:10:10,680 --> 00:10:11,680
My name is Qin Fei.

213
00:10:34,040 --> 00:10:34,970
Are you done yet?

214
00:10:35,520 --> 00:10:36,440
Dawdling.

215
00:10:41,520 --> 00:10:43,050
I heard you're hiring here.

216
00:10:43,160 --> 00:10:45,240
I thought I'd recommend myself.

217
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:47,560
At least it's an easy job.

218
00:10:52,440 --> 00:10:53,480
Listen to him.

219
00:10:53,480 --> 00:10:54,480
He's here to slack off.

220
00:10:54,480 --> 00:10:55,480
Can we hire this kind of employee?

221
00:10:55,480 --> 00:10:56,740
Is he cost-effective?

222
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:03,080
Mr. Qin, it's like this.

223
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:05,760
What we're looking for is a driver

224
00:11:05,760 --> 00:11:07,560
to pick up clients or move goods.

225
00:11:07,560 --> 00:11:09,480
If you're looking for a relaxing job,

226
00:11:09,480 --> 00:11:11,040
I'm afraid you're not suitable for this.

227
00:11:11,040 --> 00:11:11,520
Well,

228
00:11:11,720 --> 00:11:14,040
I rest when I'm free and work when there's a task.

229
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:14,800
Besides,

230
00:11:15,040 --> 00:11:16,360
I don't need a salary.

231
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:17,440
Just give me food.

232
00:11:20,040 --> 00:11:20,720
Yiyi.

233
00:11:21,880 --> 00:11:23,760
Get the contract from the second drawer.

234
00:11:23,760 --> 00:11:24,240
Okay.

235
00:11:24,240 --> 00:11:25,040
Wait a minute.

236
00:11:26,480 --> 00:11:28,040
Your place already has Lin Yiyi,

237
00:11:28,040 --> 00:11:28,960
me, and you.

238
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:31,490
Where do you have a spare room for anyone else?

239
00:11:31,680 --> 00:11:32,740
I'll live on my own.

240
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:34,690
My family owns three buildings

241
00:11:34,760 --> 00:11:36,240
just for collecting rent.

242
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:40,400
I heard Mr. Tang also works here.

243
00:11:40,960 --> 00:11:42,000
He's my tenant.

244
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:43,700
He lives right across from me.

245
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:46,160
Welcome aboard.

246
00:11:49,360 --> 00:11:50,360
Can you give me a ride later?

247
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:51,960
A client said yesterday

248
00:11:51,960 --> 00:11:54,080
that they want me to help find a shop or something.

249
00:11:54,080 --> 00:11:56,040
Zhang Yang, stay here and watch the shop.
